  "id": "lass",
  "term": "LASS",
  "definition": "LASS, or Language and Situated Simulation theory, is a view of language comprehension that involves two interacting systems: a language system and a simulation system. It proposes that understanding words and phrases often depends on mentally re-creating or imagining the experiences, objects, and situations they refer to in a context-dependent way.",
